      "id": "1381",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1381,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "ら is often called a pluralizing suffix, and is used after nouns to mean '(A) and others'. と, on the other hand, is a particle that links nouns like 'and' in English. ら can follow a single noun and implies a group with the other members not mentioned, while と connects multiple items and lists all members explicitly.",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 385,
          "slug": "ら",
          "title": "～ら",
          "meaning": "We, Them, They, These, Those",
          "level": "JLPT4",
